<Project>

  <!--
    Single source of truth for the pinned Slang release, the pinned PrismNRI release, and the pinned
    DirectXShaderCompiler release.

    Slang's public ABI is explicitly not stable (docs/design.md §3.5), so this is an exact
    pin, not a floor. Everything downstream reads it from here:

      tools/generate-native.ps1   default -SlangVersion, and the header cache path
      tools/fetch-native.ps1      which release archive to download per RID
      dotnet/PrismSlang.csproj    package metadata
      tests/                      which header the drift tests parse

    Bumping Slang is therefore: change this line, re-run both tools, run the tests, review the diff.
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <SlangVersion>v2026.14.1</SlangVersion>

    <!--
      The pinned PrismNRI release. Its GitHub release tag is `v` + this value, and the three
      packages it carries (PrismNRI, PrismNRI.Descs, PrismNRI.Testing) are what the local folder
      feed in nupkg-feed/ holds. Read by:

        tools/fetch-nri.ps1           which release to download the packages from
        nri/PrismSlang.NRI.csproj     the PrismNRI.Descs reference, in package mode (below)
        tests/PrismSlang.Tests        the PrismNRI and PrismNRI.Testing references, likewise

      Exact, like the Slang pin, and for a smaller version of the same reason: PrismNRI is
      pre-1.0 and its descriptor structs are a transcription of NRI's headers, so a minor bump can
      move a field. Bumping it is: change this line, re-run `pwsh tools/fetch-nri.ps1`, restore.
      Nothing fetches on its own; a restore against a version the feed does not hold fails with
      NU1102, which is the prompt to run the script.
    -->
    <PrismNriVersion>0.3.0-alpha</PrismNriVersion>

    <!--
      Where PrismNRI comes from: the projects of a PrismNRI checkout beside this repository when
      there is one, and the release pinned above when there is not.

      The release is the fallback and what CI builds: a runner has no PrismNRI checkout, and
      building NRI natively there would spend Actions minutes the account does not have. A
      workstation with PrismNRI checked out next to this repository builds against that checkout
      instead, as ProjectReferences, so a PrismNRI change is exercised here before it is released —
      and in October 2026 PrismNRI could not release 0.4.0-alpha at all, its Actions allowance
      spent. Read by:

        nri/PrismSlang.NRI.csproj     PrismNRI.Descs: the checkout's project, or the pinned package
        tests/PrismSlang.Tests        PrismNRI and PrismNRI.Testing, the same way

      PrismNriRoot is the checkout: the folder PrismNRI next to this repository's root unless it is
      set, as a property (-p:PrismNriRoot=...) or as an environment variable of the same name,
      absolute or relative to this file, with or without the trailing separator. PrismNriSource is
      `project` when that folder holds dotnet\PrismNRI.csproj and `package` when it does not, and
      -p:PrismNriSource=package takes the release even beside a checkout. PrismNriRootFull is the
      root made absolute, which is what the references use.

      The fallback is silent by nature: a git worktree, a runner or any other folder layout simply
      has no sibling and builds against the release. So every build says which one it took, once,
      from ReportPrismNriSource below.

      In project mode PrismNRI's managed projects build into the checkout's own obj\ and bin\, and
      its native library has to be built there already: PrismNRI.csproj stops the build with
      PRISMNRI001 when it is not, naming the commands to run in the checkout. And PrismSlang.NRI
      refuses to pack in project mode, because pack would turn the ProjectReference into a
      dependency on whatever PrismNRI.Descs version the checkout carries — unreleased, and a floor
      where the package reference is an exact pin.
    -->
    <PrismNriRoot Condition="'$(PrismNriRoot)' == ''">$([MSBuild]::NormalizeDirectory('$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)', '..', 'PrismNRI'))</PrismNriRoot>
    <PrismNriRootFull>$([MSBuild]::NormalizeDirectory('$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)', '$(PrismNriRoot)'))</PrismNriRootFull>
    <PrismNriSource Condition="'$(PrismNriSource)' == '' and Exists('$(PrismNriRootFull)dotnet\PrismNRI.csproj')">project</PrismNriSource>
    <PrismNriSource Condition="'$(PrismNriSource)' == ''">package</PrismNriSource>

    <!--
      The pinned Microsoft.Direct3D.DXC package, for PrismSlang.Native.Dxc only. Slang compiles to
      DXIL by loading dxc as a downstream compiler, by name, from the library search path — the same
      way it loads slang-glslang — and Slang's own release ships neither dxcompiler.dll nor dxil.dll.
      So a D3D12 consumer either brings dxc itself or takes the opt-in package, which copies it into
      the application's output, where PrismSlang loads it from before Slang asks for it by name.

      That package carries no binary. It depends on Microsoft's own NuGet package of dxc at exactly
      this version and copies the two DLLs out of it; the first version repackaged them from the
      DirectXShaderCompiler GitHub release, and Microsoft's licence terms in that release forbid a
      stand-alone offering of the files, which a payload-only package is. Read by:

        native/PrismSlang.Native.Dxc.csproj          the PackageReference, as an exact range
        native/build/PrismSlang.Native.Dxc.targets   restated there as the path to copy from, since
                                                     NuGet hands a consumer no path property for a
                                                     transitive package; DocumentedFactsTests pins
                                                     the two to each other
        tests/PrismSlang.Tests                       the same reference and import, so the DXIL
                                                     tests find dxc beside the compiler

      1.9.2609.5 was the newest non-prerelease version on 2026-10-14 (1.10.2605.37-preview is newer
      by date and marked preview); it is the same build as the v1.9.2609 GitHub release, and the
      DLLs report file version 1.9.2609.5. Measured with it: Slang 2026.14.1 reports dxc available,
      compiles the corpus to DXIL, and a compute shader dispatched on D3D12 through the NRI
      projection reads back correctly.

      Bumping it is: change this line and the one in the targets file, restore, run the DXIL tests.
    -->
    <DxcPackageVersion>1.9.2609.5</DxcPackageVersion>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    Which PrismNRI this build took, said once per build at high importance, so it shows at the
    default verbosity. Said by PrismSlang.NRI alone because every build that involves PrismNRI builds
    it — the tests and the reader-only consumer both reference it — where saying it from every
    project that imports this file would say it nine times. Before BeforeBuild, so it comes before
    the references are resolved: an unknown PrismNriSource, or `project` with no checkout to take
    it from, stops here with the reason rather than as a reference that resolves to nothing.
  -->
  <Target Name="ReportPrismNriSource" BeforeTargets="BeforeBuild" Condition="'$(MSBuildProjectName)' == 'PrismSlang.NRI'">
    <Error Condition="'$(PrismNriSource)' != 'project' and '$(PrismNriSource)' != 'package'"
           Text="PrismNriSource is '$(PrismNriSource)'. It is 'project', for the PrismNRI checkout at PrismNriRoot, or 'package', for the $(PrismNriVersion) release from nupkg-feed." />
    <Error Condition="'$(PrismNriSource)' == 'project' and !Exists('$(PrismNriRootFull)dotnet\PrismNRI.csproj')"
           Text="PrismNriSource is 'project', but $(PrismNriRootFull) holds no dotnet\PrismNRI.csproj. Point PrismNriRoot at a PrismNRI checkout, or build with -p:PrismNriSource=package." />

    <PropertyGroup>
      <_PrismNriReport Condition="'$(PrismNriSource)' == 'project'">PrismNRI: the projects of the checkout at $(PrismNriRootFull) (PrismNriSource=project)</_PrismNriReport>
      <_PrismNriReport Condition="'$(PrismNriSource)' == 'package' and Exists('$(PrismNriRootFull)dotnet\PrismNRI.csproj')">PrismNRI: the $(PrismNriVersion) release packages from nupkg-feed (PrismNriSource=package, set explicitly; the checkout at $(PrismNriRootFull) is not used)</_PrismNriReport>
      <_PrismNriReport Condition="'$(PrismNriSource)' == 'package' and !Exists('$(PrismNriRootFull)dotnet\PrismNRI.csproj')">PrismNRI: the $(PrismNriVersion) release packages from nupkg-feed (PrismNriSource=package; no PrismNRI checkout at $(PrismNriRootFull))</_PrismNriReport>
    </PropertyGroup>
    <Message Importance="high" Text="$(_PrismNriReport)" />
  </Target>

</Project>
